s="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8275305</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source name="APP" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1193101A1</text><sources><source name="APP" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISSAN DIESEL</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKAZAKI AKIHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISSAN DIESEL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKAZAKI, AKIHITO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKAZAKI AKIHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKAZAKI, AKIHITO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A hybrid vehicle including an engine and a motor generator to serve as a power source, comprising a clutch for automatically establishing and cutting off the transmitting of rotation between the output shaft of the engine and the input shaft of the transmission, a power transmission mechanism for transmitting power between the input/output shaft of the motor generator and the input shaft of the transmission, and a hybrid control unit for disengaging the clutch and driving the motor generator depending on the operating conditions. Depending on the operating conditions, it is possible to disengage the clutch and speed-change the rotation of the motor generator by the transmission so as to drive the vehicle, thereby enlarging the region where the motor generator operates efficiently, improving the fuel consumption reduction effect for the hybrid vehicle.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un véhicule hybride comportant: un moteur et une génératrice servant de sources de puissance; un embrayage établissant ou interrompant la transmission du couple entre l'arbre de sortie du moteur et l'arbre d'entrée de la transmission; un mécanisme de transmission de couple entre l'arbre d'entrée/sortie de la génératrice et l'arbre d'entrée de la transmission; et une unité hybride de commande désaccouplant l'embrayage et commandant la génératrice en fonction des conditions d'utilisation. Selon ces dernières, on peut désaccoupler l'embrayage et faire varier le régime de la génératrice agissant sur la transmission pour propulser le véhicule, ce qui élargit la zone de fonctionnement efficace de la génératrice et réduit la consommation de carburant du véhicule.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>